---
import CodeBlock from '../CodeBlock.astro';
import StepCard from '../StepCard.astro';
---

<div class="sec" id="s6">
  <div class="num">06</div>
  <h2>Optional: review a change in Delta</h2>
  <p class="lede">
    Your website already works. Skip this entire section unless you want to try
    Delta's visual review tools.
  </p>
  <p>
    Delta is an agent app from Zed with a different safety model. Isolated
    Workspace gives a thread a separate working copy; Existing Local Checkout
    edits your selected project directly. Check the Work In selection: a new
    thread can inherit your previous choice.
  </p>
  <p>
    Neither choice is a security sandbox. Delta's
    <a href="https://delta.dev/docs/privacy-and-security/agentic-safety"
      >safety docs</a
    >
    say agents can access the device where they run and call tools without asking,
    including destructive actions. Unlike Claude Code, Delta has no agent permission
    system. Asking for a plan is not enforced approval.
  </p>
  <p>
    Project contents and history <a
      href="https://delta.dev/docs/privacy-and-security/data-storage"
      >sync to Delta's servers</a
    > when you add a project. Agent requests may also send relevant messages and file
    contents to your selected model provider, not automatically every file in the
    repository. Use only material you are comfortable uploading. Backups outside the
    project help recovery, but cannot undo disclosure.
  </p>
  <p>
    Follow Delta's <a href="https://delta.dev/docs/installation"
      >setup instructions</a
    >
    and check <a href="https://delta.dev/docs/agents/models-and-providers"
      >model access</a
    >
    and costs before paying. Do not assume your Claude subscription also provides
    model access in Delta.
  </p>
  <div class="steps">
    <StepCard number="1" title={'Prepare and open the working copy'}>
      <p>
        Delta works with Git repositories, folders with saved change history.
        Its <a href="https://delta.dev/docs/concepts/worktrees"
          >workspace docs</a
        >
        specify a configured origin remote, another location for that history. Treat
        that as a prerequisite here. If your practice project has only local history,
        or no Git setup, stop this exercise and ask me. Do not publish files just
        to satisfy Delta.
      </p>
      <p>
        If that prerequisite is already met, follow the
        <a href="https://delta.dev/docs/getting-started/quick-start"
          >Quick Start</a
        >
        to add the top-level <code class="i">my-site-delta</code> folder, not its
        photos folder. You do not need Git commands for this review. Close Claude
        Code first.
      </p>
      <p>
        For this exercise, deliberately select Work In → Existing Local Checkout
        so the browser opens the same files you are editing. This changes <code
          class="i">my-site-delta</code
        > directly, not your backup. Run only one agent at a time.
      </p>
    </StepCard>
  </div>
  <CodeBlock
    label={'One small change'}
    code={'Read CLAUDE.md. Add "Maker and photographer" below my name in index.html; use style.css if needed. Change nothing else. Do not run Git commands, publish or push the project anywhere. Use only Delta\'s normal project synchronization. Show a short plan and wait for my ok before editing. Then list changed files and checks.'}
    copy
  />
  <div class="steps">
    <StepCard number="2" title={'Review the result'}>
      <p>
        Read the plan before replying. Open Changes with the upper-right diff
        icon to compare additions and removals (a "diff"). Select a line and
        type feedback, or send a normal message. Refresh the working copy's <code
          class="i">index.html</code
        > in your browser; check the words and narrow layout.
      </p>
      <p>
        These edits are already applied, not awaiting acceptance. Close Delta
        before restoring from backup. For help, send redacted error text, not a
        shared thread.
      </p>
    </StepCard>
  </div>
</div>
